# Hiding things (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Lies you're told"): a speaker keeps something back behind a
# default deflection in their own voice, with a Press beside it (persuade, or a threat where one is
# allowed), and a fail branch that isn't a dead end. And topics other systems put in front of you:
# the packs on the hills near a house, a voter's lean at a sitting.

conv redhand.boss.crossed
for seat:redhand/crew_boss
when tier:redhand>=known
topic "Whose line did you cross out?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say Book's the book. Lines get crossed out when they're paid, and how they got paid is between the line and me. Ask me something else.
  > @press I saw the page. Whose name was that? -> told | short   check persuade redhand 2 bg:excon
  > @lean Tell me, or I mention the second book. -> told | laughed   check threaten redhand 2
  > @back Fine. Something else. -> hub

node told
  say A lad from the bridge crew. Paid in full, Day 9. He didn't pay, mind. The infected did, on the bridge, while he was on watch for us. The book balances.
  say Don't spread it. His mother's in a Haven house and thinks he's still out on the road somewhere. Let her.
  do learn:redhand.crossed
  > @back1 I won't spread it. -> hub

node short
  say Nice try. The page is the page. Come back when you're in the book yourself, and then we'll talk about other people's lines.
  > @back2 Fine. Something else. -> hub

node laughed
  say Two books! Lads, hear this, two books. Course I keep two books. Everyone in this camp knows I keep two books. Go on, then. Tell the whole camp.
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv occupant.hills
for occupant
when tribe & !house:died
topic "What's up in the hills?"
prio world
voice haven

node start
  say? alpha :: That's {pack} again, up the hill, and {pack_leader} with them now. Since that one came they've been bolder. We keep the shutters down after dark.
  say {pack}, up the hill. That's what the houses call them. You hear them at dusk, and you learn not to answer, and to keep the children from answering.
  > @where Where do they go in the daytime? -> day
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node day
  say Somewhere quiet. Somewhere we don't go. Nobody's been up to look, nobody's volunteering, and I wouldn't ask them to.
  say If you do go, go in daylight and come back before the lamps are lit. We'll leave the door on the latch till then.
  > @back1 I'll be back before dark. -> hub

# Topics other systems put in front of you (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Trees"): a major's sitting, heard of
# at another faction's seat while it runs. Plain gossip, never a joke in its first real day.
conv bastion.leader.haven_sitting
for stronghold:bastion
when q:every_name.summoned & !ending:every_name
topic "What's the Haven voting on?"
prio world
voice bastion

node start
  say The Haven's council is voting on who eats, house by house. Show of hands round a pot. We'd use a register and a ration card.
  say If they want our cards, the template's on the wall. Nobody's asked. They'd rather argue than be counted, and I half understand it.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv redhand.leader.haven_sitting
for stronghold:redhand
when q:every_name.summoned & !ending:every_name
topic "What's the Haven voting on?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say The Haven's voting on dinner. Who eats, who works, who gets the bowl first. Lovely people. I've got odds on the pot, if you're interested.
  say Whatever they decide, somebody's hungry by Thursday. Somebody always is. That's where we come in, with tins, at a price.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub
